-- title:
--   Snapper polynomial has degree < r for r sections without common zero
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field and let $\pi\colon V\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ be a proper morphism of schemes. Let $K$ be an ordered affine cover of $V$, i.e. a finite linearly ordered index family of open subsets $U_i\subseteq V$, each affine, with $\bigsqcup_i U_i=\top$, and let $L$ be an $\mathcal{O}_V$-module satisfying the local triviality hypothesis `hL`: every point of $V$ lies in an open $U$ such that the pullback of $L$ along $U\hookrightarrow V$ is isomorphic to the unit module on $U$. Let $r\in\mathbb{N}$ and let $s\colon \mathrm{Fin}\,r\to(\mathbf{1}\to L)$ be an $r$-tuple of global sections of $L$, that is, morphisms from the unit $\mathcal{O}_V$-module to $L$. Let $G$ be an `OModulePresheaf` over $\pi$: an assignment of an $R$-module and $\Gamma(V,U)$-module structure (compatibly, via $k\to\Gamma(V,U)$) to each open $U$, together with $k$-linear restriction maps satisfying semilinearity over the structure presheaf, reflexivity and transitivity. Assume $G$ is coherent, i.e. $G(U)$ is a finite $\Gamma(V,U)$-module for every affine open $U$; quasi-coherent, i.e. on every affine open $U$ and $f\in\Gamma(V,U)$ every section over the basic open $D(f)$ is, after multiplication by some power of $f$, a restriction from $U$, and every section over $U$ restricting to zero on $D(f)$ is annihilated by a power of $f$; and supported in a closed set $Y\subseteq V$ in the sense that $G(U)$ is a subsingleton whenever the affine open $U$ is disjoint from $Y$. Assume furthermore that $Y$ meets no point of the intersection over $i$ of the supports of the ideal sheaf data $\mathrm{zeroSchemeIdeal}(s_i)$, the infimum of all ideal sheaf data dominating, on each affine open, the ideal generated by the coefficients of $s_i$. Finally let $p\in\mathbb{Q}[X]$ be a polynomial such that for every $n\in\mathbb{N}$ the Čech Euler characteristic $\sum_j(-1)^j\dim_k\check H^j(K, G\otimes L^{\otimes n})$, computed from the $k$-dimensions of the Čech groups attached to $K$, equals $p(n)$, where $L^{\otimes n}$ is the $n$-fold tensor power of $L$ built by $L^{\otimes 0}=\mathbf{1}$, $L^{\otimes(n+1)}=L^{\otimes n}\otimes L$ and the twist is taken open by open against the sections of $L^{\otimes n}$. Then the degree of $p$ is less than $r$.
--
--   This is Kleiman's vanishing statement for intersection numbers: if $r$ global sections of an invertible sheaf have no common zero on the support of a coherent sheaf $G$, then the Snapper polynomial $n\mapsto\chi(G\otimes L^{\otimes n})$ has degree $<r$, equivalently $(L^t\cdot G)=0$ for $t\ge r$. Here it feeds the study of relative group laws on Jacobians of curves of good reduction, via [`GoodReductionJacobian.RelativeGroupLaw.coeff_eq_zero_of_not_isFinite_endKerStr_of_forall_eulerChar_tensorPow_eq`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.RelativeGroupLaw.coeff_eq_zero_of_not_isFinite_endKerStr_of_forall_eulerChar_tensorPow_eq).
